content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line. This pump is within the P-101 to P-106 group whose lines are dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS at the drive-end bearing housing, which is the Figure 3 boundary between Zone C and Zone D. Zone C covers 4.5 to 7.1 mm/s RMS and is labelled 'Restricted - plan maintenance'; Zone D covers 7.1 to 11.0 mm/s RMS and is labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. Figure 3 expressly does not identify which zone owns an exact boundary value, so the reading cannot honestly be classified as definitely Zone C or definitely Zone D. Because Zone D is the manufacturer's highest severity zone, the safe planning decision is to stop the pump and obtain reliability review rather than assume the less severe classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The applicable monitoring method is vibration velocity measured on both bearing housings, with the highest reading classified using Figure 3. Only the drive-end reading is reported, so the non-drive-end reading and complete asset classification remain outstanding.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature is 72 C. The HF-300 limits that apply are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C; bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface. Thus 72 C is 2 C above the normal limit, but 8 C below alarm and 18 C below trip. It does not meet SSP-07's temperature-based requirement for a priority-1 work order, which applies only above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment: investigate first because it is listed as a probable cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature; it is not yet confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear: also common to both reported symptoms and therefore a primary inspection candidate; the drive-end measurement location alone does not prove which bearing is defective.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing: a documented possible cause of high bearing temperature; check grease quantity before adding or removing grease.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage: a documented possible cause of the high vibration requiring impeller inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation: a documented possible cause of high vibration; investigate by checking NPSH rather than assuming it from the vibration reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-103 immediately as a precaution and keep it stopped. Notify the reliability engineer before any restart and record the disposition of the exact 7.1 mm/s RMS boundary reading. The P1 and immediate-stop decision is driven by possible Zone D vibration, not by the temperature, which remains below alarm.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump or on its seal, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting the line.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "With the pump safely isolated, record diagnostic findings: check grease quantity, check alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller for wear, imbalance or damage, and check NPSH and evidence of cavitation. Do not authorise parts replacement solely from the two condition readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If internal access requires removal of the rotating assembly, use the HF-300 back pull-out arrangement, which allows removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so prepare the required signed lifting plan and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing wear is confirmed, replace the bearings as a pair using HF3-512 at the drive end and HF3-510 at the non-drive end. If M12 bearing-housing bolts are disturbed, tighten them to 85 Nm with lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C11",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the alignment check confirms misalignment, perform laser alignment and recheck the installation before return to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not schedule seal replacement merely because the pump is being inspected; no seal leak is reported. If a separate inspection finding requires seal work on this serial, do not fit HF3-450. Fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, with no sleeve measurement needed for seal setting, and tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm rather than the manual's superseded 25 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any other fasteners actually disturbed, use Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm and M24 impeller nut 160 Nm. If the casing is opened, replace casing gasket HF3-120; normal back pull-out removal does not itself require disturbing the casing.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, complete the reliability-engineer notification and document whether the pump may be tested. At the next authorised operation, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading. If 7.1 mm/s RMS recurs, retain the conservative stop pending a documented boundary interpretation. Thereafter, maintain the manual's weekly two-housing vibration monitoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional spare only; fit when inspection confirms bearing wear and pair replacement is authorised, not automatically from the vibration reading.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional spare only; fit as the other bearing of the authorised replacement pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Possible highest-zone vibration: stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. This control is being applied conservatively because the reading is exactly on the unresolved Zone C/Zone D boundary.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For internal pump or seal work: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For work on this chemically dosed line, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves; P-103 is in the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed P-101 to P-106 group.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the 68 kg back pull-out assembly or another component over 25 kg is lifted, use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any authorised run or test, maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment, if required by the alignment findings: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair, only if wear is confirmed: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If both bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment are authorised, the listed standards total 7.5 task-hours and 13.5 technician-hours. This excludes diagnostics, isolation, lifting and any additional work for which no standard time is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement is not included in the present repair total. If a separate confirmed seal scope is added, its standard allowance is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, using the serial-specific seal requirements in SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland-torque conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, and manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead prohibits HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and requires pre-set cartridge HF3-450B at 30 Nm. P-103 is serial HF3-22410 and therefore falls inside the bulletin range. For seal work governed by the bulletin, use HF3-450B and 30 Nm; the old HF3-450/25 Nm instructions continue only for pumps below HF3-22000. The bulletin also requires sleeve HF3-455 replacement when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. This decision controls any later seal work but does not create a seal-replacement requirement from the current no-leak report.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which severity zone formally owns a reading of exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS: Zone C or Zone D? Figure 3 explicitly leaves boundary ownership unresolved. Obtain the manufacturer or site reliability disposition before treating a repeated 7.1 reading as acceptable for continued operation [C07].",
    "What is the non-drive-end housing vibration, and what are the repeat drive-end readings under documented operating conditions? The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified, but only one reading is supplied [C06].",
    "What do the alignment, bearing, impeller, grease-quantity and NPSH checks show? Those findings are needed to select the actual cause, confirm whether the conditional bearing spares are required, and determine whether any impeller or other repair is necessary [C09].",
    "The evidence does not provide the correct grease quantity or grease specification, the available/required NPSH values, or a separate numerical NPSH acceptance limit. Obtain these before adjusting grease or declaring cavitation confirmed or excluded [C02, C09].",
    "Will inspection require seal disturbance, shaft-sleeve replacement, impeller replacement or casing opening? Until that is known, HF3-450B, HF3-455, HF3-210 and HF3-120 are not authorised as automatic replacements; their use is conditional on the relevant inspection findings and scope [C05, C09, C13]."
  ]
}
